From cd644233cfdc40b4b8da942c49b924b25dee2f45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rfishback <rfishback@anduril.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 12:58:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx708: add 2x2-binned and binned-cropped modes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add two register tables alongside the existing 4608x2592@14fps mode:

- imx708_mode_2304x1296_56fps[]: 2x2 binned, full FOV. Up to 56 fps at
  link freq 450 MHz. Ported from RPi rpi-6.18.y mode_2x2binned_regs[]
  with link_450Mhz_regs[] folded in (0x030E=0x01, 0x030F=0x2c).

- imx708_mode_1536x864_90fps[]: 2x2 binned, center-cropped to 720p
  active area. Sensor can run up to ~120 fps at link freq 453 MHz
  (vblank_min=40 in RPi imx708.c), but DT advertises 90 fps for CSI/VI
  margin — Tegracam writes FRM_LENGTH from DT, so the advertised max is
  the rate the sensor actually sees. Ported from RPi
  mode_2x2binned_720p_regs[] with link_453Mhz_regs[] folded in
  (0x030E=0x01, 0x030F=0x2e).

Driver source is unchanged: imx708_set_mode() already dispatches via
mode_table[s_data->mode], and timing math reads line_length /
pix_clk_hz from per-mode DT properties.

The IMX708_MODE_* enum and mode_table[] grow accordingly. The
imx708_frmfmt[] array gains two entries with their respective
fixed-frame-rate lists.
